# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# One maintainer today, so every line names the same person. The file exists
# anyway: it is the place the answer goes when that stops being true, and a
# contributor can see who will read their pull request before they open it.
#
# Last match wins, so the specific lines are below the general one.

*                           @psmux

# The pipeline. A change here can stop somebody's broadcast, so it is the one
# area where a review is not a formality.
/src/mixer.rs               @psmux
/src/input.rs               @psmux
/src/output.rs              @psmux
/src/probe.rs               @psmux

# The public contract. Changing any of these changes what every client and
# every plugin can rely on.
/src/control.rs             @psmux
/src/state.rs               @psmux
/godwinmix.example.toml     @psmux

# Packaging, CI and the documentation front door.
/deploy/                    @psmux
/.github/                   @psmux
/docs/                      @psmux
/README.md                  @psmux
/SECURITY.md                @psmux
